            "subject": "LU-21061 lod: keep default LMV pool for subdirectories"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 20:08:46.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-11-03 23:26:36.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 llite: keep default LMV pool when inheriting",
        "message": "LU-21061 llite: keep default LMV pool when inheriting\n\nWith implicit inheritance the client makes the default LMV of a\nsubdirectory that has none on disk, such as one that existed before\nits parent got a default.  The client drops it once max_inherit runs\nout, so mkdir deep in such a tree is no longer limited to the MDTs\nof the pool.\n\nAdd lmv_inherit_default() to make the default a subdirectory\ninherits the same way the MDT does: a parent default that stops\ninheriting still passes on its pool, with a single stripe on any\nMDT and unlimited inheritance.  Use it in\nll_dir_default_lmv_inherit() and lmv_object_inherited(), which now\nalso compares pools.\n\nAlso give an \"lfs mkdir\" layout that names no pool the pool of the\nparent default in ll_dir_setdirstripe(), so that the MDT allocates\nits stripes from the same pool.\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I88082f8306de246fbb3c2d1167939c93c1061266\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
